{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGf6dSTMtjpyd4HeriRy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I recorded the work in Warrant and exported a handoff package. The duty is still open.\n\n**What's recorded**\n- The transition is `1c03acb020da506f5ae254991267d417c04fcbcfb4cf83354920359fb0345b48`, committed in workspace `main`.\n- It says `parse_amount()` now handles negative amounts, so \"-12.50\" parses to -1250 cents. `test_negative` and `test_zero` passed. These are marked ATTESTED, meaning they are my report and nobody has replayed them.\n- It lists three things as still open. Thousands separators such as \"-1,200.00\" still fail and are the next step. I haven't checked the other formats in `docs/amount-formats.md`. The duty is not closed.\n- The duty is `aaf4459f8c5012a3af39a4f0a106b7d8fa60cd729de7af85a6443e37bfca5bd9`.\n\n**What to pass to the next agent**\n1. The package object from the `warrant_handoff` export, passed as it is. Its `manifest`, `payload` and `declaration` fields must arrive unchanged. I called the export with the transition and duty ids as roots. It holds 2 records and no blobs.\n2. The manifest digest, so they can check what they received: `bb4ede54c80afa50f93b8bec6b01a7a44c05ffc0f85cd4225384d190534e8b5a`.\n3. A note that completeness is UNATTESTED, so the package doesn't prove it is the whole store.\n\nThe next agent should run `warrant_handoff op=inspect` on the package. They should use their own configured expectation handle, because without one the delivery shows as UNPINNED. If it looks right, they import it with the `staged_id` from the inspect result. Then they continue with the thousands-separator case.\n\n**Code is not included**\nThe package carries only Warrant records. It doesn't include my edit to `billing/parse.py`, and this directory isn't a git repository. The other machine has its own copy, so you need to get that edit across yourself, for example as a copy of the file or a diff. If you don't, the next agent will start from the unchanged parser, and the record will describe a change they can't see.\n\nI couldn't print the package here without losing bytes. If you want, I can re-run the export and save it to a file for you to copy."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5200,"cache_read_input_tokens":10955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5200},"output_tokens":723,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73e09849-c9b6-4ddc-be48-15632ffa0dd7","uuid":"925d7056-74ad-466f-85cf-c139ec180e16","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:38:29.899Z","request_id":"req_011CgGf6dB62s9GxPvBipFvL"}
